	(text "HP-SDI12-NANO / COMPACT FLAT   -   11.5-14.4 V battery supply over the 3-wire SDI-12 cable. J1 has three bare cable solder holes (VIN, data,\nground); no connector is fitted. 5 V comes from a buck converter (TI LMR36503R5, 5 V fixed, ~4 uA no-load, 2.2 MHz with RT tied to GND), which\nwastes several times less heat than a linear regulator."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 31.8 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "b7c1d555-d29f-4af4-9b03-eca9a32984ca")
	)
	(text "SDI-12 DATA   -   meets the SDI-12 electrical numbers: R3 sets the 1-2 k\ntransmit resistance (and limits fault current into pin D2), R4 the\n160-360 k idle resistance, C4 holds the edge rate under 1.5 V/us. D4\nclamps cable transients."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 285 32.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "28c9936c-65fc-4897-a5f1-56973af42005")
	)
	(text "MICROCONTROLLER   -   Renesas RA4M1 (R7FA4M1AB3CFM), the Arduino UNO R4 / Nano R4 chip, wired exactly like the UNO R4 Minima so the stock\nboard package and Arduino pin names apply (nets D2, D4, D9, A0-A5). Runs at 5 V. Support circuit (NMI, USB sense, VCC_USB, VCL) follows\nArduino's Nano R4 schematic. No 32.768 kHz crystal: the stock Arduino core clocks the CPU and USB from the internal HOCO and the RTC from\nLOCO."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 128.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "dcbd3b22-5bc8-4ea7-9612-6beebafd0c7a")
	)
	(text "FIRMWARE ACCESS (no soldering)   -   J2 is a row of five holes for an off-the-shelf 2.54 mm 5-pin pogo clip. Holes 1-4 carry USB (5V, D-, D+,\nGND): plug a 'USB to 4-pin Dupont' cable onto the clip and the board is an 'Arduino UNO R4 Minima' in the IDE. Hole 5 = BOOT: only for the\nvery first load of the Arduino bootloader, put a jumper cap across clip pins 4-5 while plugging in. Recovery never needs a programmer: with\nthe BOOT jumper fitted, the chip's built-in USB boot mode reloads the bootloader over the same clip."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 320.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "3a6d8a72-eba7-4103-b30c-982def96b50f")
	)
	(text "HEATER DRIVE + POWER MONITOR   -   PWM-capable D9/P303 drives Q1. Required\nfirmware: 100 Hz, nominal 2 W average, 8-15 s; integrate stable ON power times\nactual ON time. Force D9 LOW at shutdown; stopping a timer is insufficient. R10\npulls an undriven gate LOW. Keep all three INA226 inputs on their dedicated\nKelvin connections. Firmware is not included."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430 23.6 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "54e044bd-3262-4c2d-a14d-13655a161851")
	)
	(text "HEATER RESISTOR CHAIN (top of center prong)   -   17 x 3.3 ohm 1% 0603 in series, 2.6 mm pitch. EXACT Vishay CRCW06033R30FKEAHP, 0.33 W at 70 C; no ordinary 0.1 W substitutes. Return is on bottom copper. Nominal full-ON power 2.34 W at 12 V, 3.41 W at 14.4 V with specified cable losses. PWM\ncontrols average energy; instantaneous ratings still apply. Qualify the potted needle thermally."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 368.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "4667ab43-abcb-4030-ab3b-71c5370cb79e")
	)
	(text "THERMISTORS   -   pin map (same on flat-nano and hat): A2 = TH1 right needle, A1\n= TH2 heater-needle tip, A0 = TH3 left needle, A3 = TH4 board body (left/right\nseen on the top face, cable end up, needles down). Required firmware: 14-bit ADC,\nexternal VREF (AR_EXTERNAL), 64 readings averaged; actual noise and accuracy\nrequire measurement. The dividers and ADC reference share VREF. D4 powers the\ndividers AND the ADC reference through R11, so they are off between readings (no\nself-heating) and the reading stays ratiometric. Sequence: D4 HIGH, wait 10 ms,\nread, D4 LOW. R_ntc = Rref * code / (full scale - code). NTC = Murata\nNCP15XH103F03RC (10k, 1%); Rref = 10k 0.1% 25 ppm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430 187.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "6d43b533-3f64-4680-8d59-fa3295378578")
	)
